  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nHigh pressure will continue to be situated across the Northern Great \nLakes through early next week bringing dry and seasonal weather to \nthe region. There's a strong low pressure currently off the east \ncoast that will stall over the next couple of days and slowly drift \nto the west. This will briefly increase PoP chances across NW PA lat \nSunday evening into early Monday morning when the low will weaken \nand move off to the northeast. The next chance for widespread \nprecipitation will be mid to late week. There's still plenty of \nspread within the models with timing, so it's difficult to pin point \nwhen the onset will be. Until then, pleasant seasonal weather will \nbe across the region with highs in the mid 60 to low 70s and \novernight lows in the upper 40s to mid 50s.",
